## Code Quality & Modernization
### MathExt Refactoring ✅ COMPLETE
- [x] Remove duplicate Min/Max/Clamp methods from MathExt
  - Replaced all MathExt.Min calls with Math.Min (~30 files)
  - Replaced all MathExt.Max calls with Math.Max
  - Replaced all MathExt.Clamp calls with Math.Clamp
  - Kept CssUI-specific utilities: Feq, Fgteq, Flteq, DegreesToRadians, RangeClamp
  - RangeClamp preserved (handles min>max case unlike Math.Clamp)

### Type System Modernization
- [x] Analyze unit type structures in codebase
  - Audit: Point2f, Point2i, Point3f, Rect2f, Rect2i, Rect4f, Rect4i, Size2f, etc.
  - Evaluate replacement with System.Numerics types (Vector2, Vector3, etc.)
  - Consider System.Drawing types where appropriate
  - Document migration plan if beneficial

### Standard Library Alignment ✅ ANALYZED
See [PARSING_ANALYSIS.md](CssUI/docs/PARSING_ANALYSIS.md) for detailed analysis.

- [x] Analyze integer/numeric parsing implementations
  - Custom parsing in ParsingCommon.cs, Numerics.cs, CssTokenizer.cs
  - HTML spec allows trailing non-digits (parsing stops); .NET throws
  - CSS tokenizer needs stream-based parsing with token type output
  - **Conclusion: Custom implementations required for spec compliance**
- [x] Analyze string parsing implementations
  - StringCommon.cs: StrEq/StriEq already use .NET StringComparison
  - ASCII whitespace (5 chars) differs from .NET Unicode whitespace
  - Memory-efficient Span<char>/ReadOnlyMemory<char> operations needed
  - **Conclusion: Custom implementations required for spec compliance**

